\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces When and why the single-predictor bridge breaks down. \textit  {(a)} Partial correlation of each halo-level quantity with $S(\ell )$ (at fixed $f_{\rm  gas}$) vs.\ $\ell $: thermal quantities ($c_{\rm  gas}$, $\log Y$, $\log K$) dominate below $\ell \sim 1500$, structural quantities ($c_{\rm  DM}$, $f_\star $) above. \textit  {(b)} The two-variable $f_{\rm  gas}+c_{\rm  DM}$ bridge (green) restores the correlation with $S(\ell )$ relative to the $f_{\rm  gas}$-only bridge (black), especially at high $\ell $. \textit  {(c)} The mean residual $S-{\rm  bridge}(f_{\rm  gas})$ by feedback family, showing AGN runs above and SN/wind runs below the bridge at high $\ell $. \textcolor {red}{[TODO: this figure's own family-classification legend (AGN $n=18$, SN/wind $n=31$, other $n=8$) does not match the classification used in Figure~\ref {fig:bridge_fgas} (AGN $20$, SN/wind $25$, other $12$) for the apparently identical 57-run 1P design; we have not been able to reconcile which classification script is authoritative from the source material available, and flag this discrepancy explicitly rather than silently pick one.]}}}{14}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bridge_residual}{{10}{14}{When and why the single-predictor bridge breaks down. \textit {(a)} Partial correlation of each halo-level quantity with $\Sell $ (at fixed $\fgas $) vs.\ $\ell $: thermal quantities ($c_{\rm gas}$, $\log Y$, $\log K$) dominate below $\ell \sim 1500$, structural quantities ($c_{\rm DM}$, $f_\star $) above. \textit {(b)} The two-variable $\fgas +c_{\rm DM}$ bridge (green) restores the correlation with $\Sell $ relative to the $\fgas $-only bridge (black), especially at high $\ell $. \textit {(c)} The mean residual $S-{\rm bridge}(\fgas )$ by feedback family, showing AGN runs above and SN/wind runs below the bridge at high $\ell $. \todo {this figure's own family-classification legend (AGN $n=18$, SN/wind $n=31$, other $n=8$) does not match the classification used in Figure~\ref {fig:bridge_fgas} (AGN $20$, SN/wind $25$, other $12$) for the apparently identical 57-run 1P design; we have not been able to reconcile which classification script is authoritative from the source material available, and flag this discrepancy explicitly rather than silently pick one.}}{figure.10}{}}
